insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$ankle-injuries-and-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1612$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Ankle Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Ankle Injuries and Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A broad category of ankle harm rather than one diagnosis; specific entities like ankle fracture or sprain are the case-suitable topics.", "kind": "other", "category": "musculoskeletal injury category", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["emergency", "clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your ankle bone and the ends of your two lower leg bones make up the ankle joint. Your ligaments, which connect bones to one another, stabilize and support it. Your muscles and tendons move it.
The most common ankle problems are sprains and fractures (broken bones). A sprain is an injury to the ligaments. It may take a few weeks to many months to heal completely. A fracture is a break in a bone. You can also injure other parts of the ankle such as tendons, which join muscles to bone, and cartilage, which cushions your joints. Ankle sprains and fractures are common sports injuries.
MeSH definition (Ankle Injuries): Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.
MeSH definition (Ankle Fractures): Fractures of any of the bones of the ANKLE.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Arm Injuries and Disorders, Chest Injuries and Disorders, Foot Injuries and Disorders, Head Injuries, Knee Injuries and Disorders, Leg Injuries and Disorders, Osteoporosis, Shoulder Injuries and Disorders, Spine Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$)
