insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$arm-injuries-and-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-4329$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Arm Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Arm Injuries and Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A broad category of arm harm rather than a single diagnosis; specific fractures or nerve injuries are the case-suitable topics.", "kind": "other", "category": "musculoskeletal injury category", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["emergency", "clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Of the 206 bones in your body, three of them are in your arm: the humerus, radius, and ulna. Your arms are also made up of muscles, joints, tendons, and other connective tissue. Injuries to any of these parts of the arm can occur during sports, a fall, or an accident.
Types of arm injuries include :
- Tendinitis and bursitis
- Sprains
- Dislocations
- Fractures (broken bones)
- Nerve problems
- Osteoarthritis
You may also have problems or injure specific parts of your arm, such as your hand, wrist, elbow, or shoulder.
MeSH definition (Humeral Fractures): Fractures of the HUMERUS.
MeSH definition (Arm Injuries): General or unspecified injuries involving the UPPER ARM and the FOREARM.
MeSH definition (Ulna Fractures): Fractures of the larger bone of the forearm.
MeSH definition (Radius Fractures): Fractures of the RADIUS.
MeSH definition (Arm): The superior part of the upper extremity between the SHOULDER and the ELBOW.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Animal Bites, Ankle Injuries and Disorders, Back Injuries, Barotrauma, Burns, Chest Injuries and Disorders, Dislocations, Drowning, Elbow Injuries and Disorders, Electrical Injuries, Foreign Bodies, Fractures, Frostbite, Hand Injuries and Disorders, Head Injuries$rounds_kb$)
