insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$back-injuries$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-156$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Back Injuries$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Back Injuries", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A mechanism-based category rather than a diagnosis; students reach specific entities such as lumbar strain or vertebral fracture, which are better case topics.", "kind": "injury", "category": "musculoskeletal trauma category", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["emergency", "clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your back is made of bones, muscles, and other tissues extending from your neck to your pelvis. Back injuries can result from sports injuries, work around the house or in the garden, or a sudden jolt such as a car accident. The lower back is the most common site of back injuries and back pain. Common back injuries include :
- Sprains and strains
- Herniated disks
- Fractured (broken) vertebrae
These injuries can cause pain and limit your movement. Treatments vary but might include medicines, icing, bed rest, physical therapy, or surgery. You might be able to prevent some back injuries by maintaining a healthy weight, lifting objects with your legs, and using lower-back support when you sit.
MeSH definition (Back Injuries): General or unspecified injuries to the posterior part of the trunk. It includes injuries to the muscles of the back.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Animal Bites, Arm Injuries and Disorders, Barotrauma, Burns, Chest Injuries and Disorders, Dislocations, Drowning, Electrical Injuries, Foreign Bodies, Fractures, Frostbite, Hand Injuries and Disorders, Heat Illness, Hip Injuries and Disorders, Leg Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$)
