insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$bad-breath$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-6033$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Bad Breath$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Bad Breath", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Common complaint with a focused differential (oral hygiene, gingival disease, sinus or GI causes); diagnosis largely by history and exam, though the presentation is less classic for a full case.", "kind": "symptom", "category": "oral / ENT symptom", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$There are many reasons why you might have bad breath. You can get it if you don't brush and floss regularly. Bacteria that build up in your mouth and between your teeth produce the bad odor. Other problems in your mouth, such as gum disease, dry mouth, or cavities, may also cause it. Sinusitis or problems with your nose may be to blame. You can also have bad breath if you eat some foods, like raw onions, garlic, or cabbage. And of course smoking causes its own bad smell. Some diseases and medicines can cause a specific breath odor.
Having good dental habits, like brushing and flossing regularly, help fight bad breath. Mouthwashes, mints or chewing gum may make your breath fresher. If you have a disease that causes the bad breath, treating the disease may help give you fresher breath.
MeSH definition (Halitosis): An offensive, foul breath odor resulting from a variety of causes such as poor oral hygiene, dental or oral infections, or the ingestion of certain foods.
Also called: Halitosis
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Abdominal Pain, Bowel Incontinence, Constipation, Diarrhea, Eating Disorders, Gas, Heartburn, Hiccups, Indigestion, Nausea and Vomiting$rounds_kb$)
