insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$bladder-diseases$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-164$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Bladder Diseases$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$renal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Bladder Diseases", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of bladder pathology, not a single diagnosis a student can reach by interview and workup.", "kind": "other", "category": "urologic disorders", "organ_systems": ["renal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The bladder is a hollow organ in your lower abdomen that stores urine. Many conditions can affect your bladder. Some common ones are:
- Cystitis - inflammation of the bladder, often from an infection
- Urinary incontinence - loss of bladder control
- Overactive bladder - a condition in which the bladder squeezes urine out at the wrong time
- Interstitial cystitis - a chronic problem that causes bladder pain and frequent, urgent urination
- Bladder cancer
Doctors diagnose bladder diseases using different tests. These include urine tests, x-rays, and an examination of the bladder wall with a scope called a cystoscope. Treatment depends on the cause of the problem. It may include medicines and, in severe cases, surgery.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Urinary Bladder Diseases): Pathological processes of the URINARY BLADDER.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Kidney Diseases, Ureteral Disorders, Urethral Disorders, Urinary Tract Infections, Urine and Urination$rounds_kb$)
