insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$bleeding-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-166$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Bleeding Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$blood$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Bleeding Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category covering many coagulopathies; not a single diagnosis reachable by interview and workup.", "kind": "other", "category": "coagulopathy", "organ_systems": ["blood"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["pediatrics", "emergency"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Normally, if you get hurt, your body forms a blood clot to stop the bleeding. For blood to clot, your body needs cells called platelets and proteins known as clotting factors. If
you have a bleeding disorder, you either do not have enough platelets or clotting factors
or they don't work the way they should.
Bleeding disorders can be the result of other diseases, such as severe liver disease or a lack of vitamin K. They can also be inherited. Hemophilia is an inherited bleeding disorder. Bleeding disorders can also be a side effect of medicines such as blood thinners.
Various blood tests can check for a bleeding disorder. You will also have a physical exam and history. Treatments depend on the cause. They may include medicines and transfusions of blood, platelets, or clotting factor.
MeSH definition (Blood Coagulation Disorders): Hemorrhagic and thrombotic disorders that occur as a consequence of abnormalities in blood coagulation due to a variety of factors such as COAGULATION PROTEIN DISORDERS; BLOOD PLATELET DISORDERS; BLOOD PROTEIN DISORDERS or nutritional conditions.
Also called: Clotting disorders
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Anemia, Blood Transfusion and Donation, Bone Marrow Diseases, Childhood Leukemia, Leukemia, Platelet Disorders, Rh Incompatibility$rounds_kb$)
