insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$bronchial-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5977$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Bronchial Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$respiratory$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Bronchial Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of bronchial diseases; not a single interviewable diagnosis.", "kind": "other", "category": "category term", "organ_systems": ["respiratory"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$When you breathe in, the air travels down through your trachea (windpipe). It then goes through two tubes to your lungs. These tubes are your bronchi. Bronchial disorders can make it hard for you to breathe.
The most common problem with the bronchi is bronchitis, an inflammation of the tubes. It can be acute or chronic. Other problems include:
- Bronchiectasis - a condition in which damage to the airways causes them to widen and become flabby and scarred
- Exercise-induced bronchospasm - a breathing problem that happens when your airways shrink while you are exercising
- Bronchiolitis - an inflammation of the small airways that branch off from the bronchi
- Bronchopulmonary dysplasia - a chronic lung condition in infants, most often premature infants
MeSH definition (Bronchial Diseases): Diseases involving the BRONCHI.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Chest Injuries and Disorders, Lung Diseases, Nose Injuries and Disorders, Pleural Disorders, Pulmonary Rehabilitation, Tracheal Disorders$rounds_kb$)
