insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$cerebellar-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5919$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Cerebellar Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Cerebellar Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of cerebellar dysfunction with many causes; not a single diagnosis a student can reach from one patient encounter.", "kind": "other", "category": "cerebellar dysfunction", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "neurology", "secondary_clerkships": [], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$When you play the piano or hit a tennis ball you are activating the cerebellum. The cerebellum is the area of the brain that controls coordination and balance. Problems with the cerebellum include:
- Cancer
- Genetic disorders
- Ataxias - failure of muscle control in the arms and legs that result in movement disorders
- Degeneration - disorders caused by brain cells decreasing in size or wasting away
Treatment of cerebellar disorders depends on the cause. In some cases, there is no cure but treatment may help with symptoms.
NIH: National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke
MeSH definition (Cerebellar Diseases): Diseases that affect the structure or function of the cerebellum. Cardinal manifestations of cerebellar dysfunction include dysmetria, GAIT ATAXIA, and MUSCLE HYPOTONIA.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Amblyopia, Brain Tumors, Childhood Brain Tumors, Dementia, Encephalitis, Epilepsy, Headache, Hydrocephalus$rounds_kb$)
