insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$colonic-diseases$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-194$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Colonic Diseases$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Colonic Diseases", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A broad organ-based category, not a specific diagnosis a student can reach by interview and workup.", "kind": "other", "category": "gastrointestinal category", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your colon, also known as the large intestine, is part of your digestive system. It's a long, hollow tube at the end of your digestive tract where your body makes and stores stool. Many disorders affect the colon's ability to work properly. Some of these include:
- Colorectal cancer
- Colonic polyps - extra tissue growing in the colon that can become cancerous
- Ulcerative colitis - ulcers of the colon and rectum
- Diverticulitis - inflammation or infection of pouches in the colon
- Irritable bowel syndrome - an uncomfortable condition causing abdominal cramping and other symptoms
Treatment for colonic diseases varies greatly depending on the disease and its severity. Treatment may involve diet, medicines and in some cases, surgery.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Colonic Diseases): Pathological processes in the COLON region of the large intestine (INTESTINE, LARGE).
Also called: Large intestine diseases
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Intestinal Obstruction, Malabsorption Syndromes, Rectal Disorders, Small Intestine Disorders$rounds_kb$)
