insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$color-blindness$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-4400$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Color Blindness$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Color Blindness", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Hereditary vision defect detected by history and simple testing; reasonable pediatric or primary care case though limited workup.", "kind": "disease", "category": "inherited sensory defect", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "pediatrics", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["pediatric_clinic", "clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Most of us see our world in color. We enjoy looking at a lush green lawn or a red rose in full bloom. If you have a color vision defect, you may see these colors differently than most people.
There are three main kinds of color vision defects. Red-green color vision defects are the most common. This type occurs in men more than in women. The other major types are blue-yellow color vision defects and a complete absence of color vision.
Most of the time, color blindness is genetic. There is no treatment, but most people adjust and the condition doesn't limit their activities.
MeSH definition (Color Vision Defects): Defects of color vision are mainly hereditary traits but can be secondary to acquired or developmental abnormalities in the CONES (RETINA). Severity of hereditary defects of color vision depends on the degree of mutation of the ROD OPSINS genes (on X CHROMOSOME and CHROMOSOME 3) that code the photopigments for red, green and blue.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Amblyopia$rounds_kb$)
