insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$coping-with-chronic-illness$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-4208$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Coping with Chronic Illness$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$very_common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$behavioral$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Coping with Chronic Illness", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A psychosocial/care concept rather than a diagnosis; no single patient presentation or workup leads to it.", "kind": "other", "category": "psychosocial care topic", "organ_systems": ["behavioral"], "primary_clerkship": "psychiatry", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Having a long-term, or chronic, illness can disrupt your life in many ways. You may often be tired and in pain. Your illness might affect your appearance or your physical abilities and independence. You may not be able to work, causing financial problems. For children, chronic illnesses can be frightening, because they may not understand why this is happening to them.
These changes can cause stress, anxiety, and anger. If they do, it is important to seek help. A trained counselor can help you develop strategies to regain a feeling of control. Support groups might help, too. You will find that you are not alone, and you may learn some new tips on how to cope.
You may be able to manage your illness better if you learn more about it. It is important to evaluate the information that you find, to make sure that it is reliable. It is also important to find a health care provider that you can trust.
MeSH definition (Chronic Disease): Diseases which have one or more of the following characteristics: they are permanent, leave residual disability, are caused by nonreversible pathological alteration, require special training of the patient for rehabilitation, or may be expected to require a long period of supervision, observation, or care (Dictionary of Health Services Management, 2d ed). For epidemiological studies chronic disease often includes HEART DISEASES; STROKE; CANCER; and diabetes (DIABETES MELLITUS, TYPE 2).
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Infectious Diseases, Rare Diseases, Winter Weather Emergencies$rounds_kb$)
