insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$corneal-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5532$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Corneal Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Corneal Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of eye disease, not a specific diagnosis a student reaches by interview and workup.", "kind": "disease", "category": "ophthalmologic disorder", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your cornea is the outermost layer of your eye. It is clear and shaped like a dome. The cornea helps to shield the rest of the eye from germs, dust, and other harmful matter. It also helps your eye to focus. If you wear contact lenses, they float on top of your corneas.
Problems with the cornea include:
- Refractive errors
- Allergies
- Infections
- Injuries
- Dystrophies - conditions in which parts of the cornea lose clarity due to a buildup of cloudy material
Treatments of corneal disorders include medicines, corneal transplantation, and corneal laser surgery.
NIH: National Eye Institute
MeSH definition (Corneal Injuries): Damage or trauma inflicted to the CORNEA by external means.
MeSH definition (Corneal Diseases): Diseases of the cornea.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Eye Cancer, Eye Care, Eye Diseases, Eye Infections, Eye Injuries, Eye Movement Disorders, Eyelid Disorders, Optic Nerve Disorders, Refractive Errors, Retinal Disorders, Tears, Vision Impairment and Blindness$rounds_kb$)
