insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$craniofacial-abnormalities$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5757$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Craniofacial Abnormalities$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Craniofacial Abnormalities", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of congenital malformations rather than one diagnosis; no single interview-and-workup path.", "kind": "disease", "category": "congenital anomaly", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "pediatrics", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["pediatric_clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Craniofacial is a medical term that relates to the bones of the skull and face. Craniofacial abnormalities are birth defects of the face or head. Some, like cleft lip and palate, are among the most common of all birth defects. Others are very rare. Most of them affect how a person's face or head looks. These conditions may also affect other parts of the body.
Treatment depends on the type of problem. Plastic and reconstructive surgery may help the person's appearance.
MeSH definition (Craniofacial Abnormalities): Congenital structural deformities, malformations, or other abnormalities of the cranium and facial bones.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Facial Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$)
