insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$dandruff-cradle-cap-and-other-scalp-conditions$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-6410$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Dandruff, Cradle Cap, and Other Scalp Conditions$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$very_common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Dandruff, Cradle Cap, and Other Scalp Conditions", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Seborrheic dermatitis is a common scalp complaint diagnosed clinically by history and skin exam, with recognizable distribution and appearance.", "kind": "disease", "category": "skin and soft tissue", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["pediatrics", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic", "pediatric_clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your scalp is the skin on the top of your head. Unless you have hair loss, hair grows on your scalp. Different skin problems can affect your scalp.
Dandruff is a flaking of the skin. The flakes are yellow or white. Dandruff may make your scalp feel itchy. It usually starts after puberty, and is more common in men. Dandruff is usually a symptom of seborrheic dermatitis, or seborrhea. It is a skin condition that can also cause redness and irritation of the skin.
Most of the time, using a dandruff shampoo can help control your dandruff. If that does not work, contact your health care provider.
There is a type of seborrheic dermatitis that babies can get. It is called cradle cap. It usually lasts a few months, and then goes away on its own. Besides the scalp, it can sometimes affect other parts of the body, such as the eyelids, armpits, groin, and ears. Normally, washing your baby's hair every day with a mild shampoo and gently rubbing their scalp with your fingers or a soft brush can help. For severe cases, your health care provider may give you a prescription shampoo or cream to use.
Other problems that can affect the scalp include:
- Scalp ringworm, a fungal infection that causes itchy, red patches on your head. It can also leave bald spots. It usually affects children.
- Scalp psoriasis, which causes itchy or sore patches of thick, red skin with silvery scales. About half of the people with psoriasis have it on their scalp.
MeSH definition (Scalp Dermatoses): Skin diseases involving the SCALP.
MeSH definition (Dermatitis, Seborrheic): A chronic inflammatory disease of the skin with unknown etiology. It is characterized by moderate ERYTHEMA, dry, moist, or greasy (SEBACEOUS GLAND) scaling and yellow crusted patches on various areas, especially the scalp, that exfoliate as dandruff. Seborrheic dermatitis is common in children and adolescents with HIV INFECTIONS.
MeSH definition (Dandruff): Excessive shedding of dry scaly material from the scalp in humans.
Also called: Seborrhea, Seborrheic Dermatitis
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Acne, Breast Diseases, Eczema, Foot Injuries and Disorders, Hair Problems, Itching, Nail Diseases, Psoriasis, Rashes, Rosacea, Scleroderma, Skin Cancer, Skin Infections, Skin Pigmentation Disorders$rounds_kb$)
