insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$diabetes-insipidus$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-3046$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Diabetes Insipidus$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$endocrine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$renal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Diabetes Insipidus", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Polyuria and polydipsia workup with a clear diagnostic path through water deprivation and ADH testing; good electrolyte differential.", "kind": "disease", "category": "water-balance disorder", "organ_systems": ["endocrine", "renal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology", "familyMedicine", "pediatrics"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["inpatient", "clinic", "icu"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Diabetes insipidus (DI) causes frequent urination. You become extremely thirsty, so you drink. Then you urinate. This cycle can keep you from sleeping or even make you wet the bed. Your body produces lots of urine that is almost all water.
DI is different from diabetes mellitus (DM), which involves insulin problems and high blood sugar. The symptoms can be similar. However, DI is related to how your kidneys handle fluids. It's much less common than DM. Urine and blood tests can show which one you have.
Usually, DI is caused by a problem with your pituitary gland or your kidneys. Treatment depends on the cause of the problem. Medicines can often help.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Diabetes Insipidus): A disease that is characterized by frequent urination, excretion of large amounts of dilute URINE, and excessive THIRST. Etiologies of diabetes insipidus include deficiency of antidiuretic hormone (also known as ADH or VASOPRESSIN) secreted by the NEUROHYPOPHYSIS, impaired KIDNEY response to ADH, and impaired hypothalamic regulation of thirst.
Also called: DI
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Diabetic Kidney Problems, Kidney Cancer, Kidney Cysts, Kidney Stones, Pituitary Tumors$rounds_kb$)
