insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$edema$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1229$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Edema$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$very_common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$cardiovascular$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$renal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Edema", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "A common symptom with a broad cardiorenal-hepatic differential that students evaluate through history, exam and labs.", "kind": "symptom", "category": "fluid overload symptom", "organ_systems": ["cardiovascular", "renal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine", "emergency"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Edema means swelling caused by fluid in your body's tissues. It usually occurs in the feet, ankles and legs, but it can involve your entire body.
Causes of edema include:
- Eating too much salt
- Sunburn
- Heart failure
- Kidney disease
- Liver problems from cirrhosis
- Pregnancy
- Problems with lymph nodes, especially after mastectomy
- Some medicines
- Standing or walking a lot when the weather is warm
To keep swelling down, your health care provider may recommend keeping your legs raised when sitting, wearing support stockings, limiting how much salt you eat, or taking a medicine called a diuretic - also called a water pill.
MeSH definition (Edema): Abnormal fluid accumulation in TISSUES or body cavities. Most cases of edema are present under the SKIN in SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUE.
Also called: Dropsy, Swelling
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Body Weight, Fatigue, Motion Sickness$rounds_kb$)
