insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$electrical-injuries$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-6280$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Electrical Injuries$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$cardiovascular$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Electrical Injuries", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "A specific injury with a defined mechanism, exam findings and management priorities that students can work through in the ED.", "kind": "injury", "category": "environmental injury", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal", "cardiovascular"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["emergency", "icu"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$When you come in direct contact with electricity, it can pass through your body and cause injuries. These electrical injuries can be external or internal. You may have one or both types. External injuries are skin burns. Internal injuries include damage to your organs, bones, muscles, and nerves. You could also have abnormal heart rhythms and sudden cardiac arrest (SCA).
How bad your injuries are depends on how strong the electric current was, what type of current it was, how it moved through your body, and how long you were exposed. Other factors include how healthy you are, and how quickly you get treatment.
Causes of electrical injuries include:
- Lightning strikes
- Faulty electrical appliances
- Work-related exposures
- Contact with household wiring or power lines
- Accidents in small children, when they bite or suck on electrical cords, or stick objects in outlets
If you get an electrical injury, you should see a doctor. You may have internal damage and not realize it.
MeSH definition (Burns, Electric): Burns produced by contact with electric current or from a sudden discharge of electricity.
MeSH definition (Electric Injuries): Injuries caused by electric currents. The concept excludes electric burns (BURNS, ELECTRIC), but includes accidental electrocution and electric shock.
Also called: Electric shock, Electrical burn
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Animal Bites, Arm Injuries and Disorders, Back Injuries, Barotrauma, Burns, Chest Injuries and Disorders, Dislocations, Drowning, Foreign Bodies, Fractures, Frostbite, Hand Injuries and Disorders, Heat Illness, Hip Injuries and Disorders, Inhalation Injuries$rounds_kb$)
