insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$esophageal-cancer$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-245$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Esophageal Cancer$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Esophageal Cancer", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Progressive dysphagia and weight loss with clear risk factors; diagnosis reachable by history and endoscopy with biopsy, with staging workup.", "kind": "disease", "category": "malignancy", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": true}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The esophagus is a hollow tube that carries food and liquids from your throat to your stomach. Early esophageal cancer usually does not cause symptoms. Later, you may have symptoms such as:
- Painful or difficult swallowing
- Weight loss
- A hoarse voice or cough that doesn't go away
You're at greater risk for getting esophageal cancer if you smoke, drink heavily, or have acid reflux. Your risk also goes up as you age
Your doctor uses imaging tests and a biopsy to diagnose esophageal cancer. Treatments include surgery, radiation, and chemotherapy. You might also need nutritional support, since the cancer or treatment may make it hard to swallow.
NIH: National Cancer Institute
MeSH definition (Esophageal Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer of the ESOPHAGUS.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Oral Cancer, Stomach Cancer, Swallowing Disorders, Thyroid Cancer$rounds_kb$)
