insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$eye-injuries$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-492$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Eye Injuries$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Eye Injuries", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Traumatic eye presentation with red eye, pain and vision change; diagnosis reachable by history, exam and imaging, with chemical burn and globe rupture as key entities.", "kind": "injury", "category": "ocular trauma", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["emergency", "clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The structure of your face helps protect your eyes from injury. Still, injuries can damage your eye, sometimes severely enough that you could lose your vision. Most eye injuries are preventable. If you play sports or work in certain jobs, you may need protection.
The most common type of injury happens when something irritates the outer surface of your eye. Certain jobs such as industrial jobs or hobbies such as carpentry make this type of injury more likely. It's also more likely if you wear contact lenses.
Chemicals or heat can burn your eyes. With chemicals, the pain may cause you to close your eyes. This traps the irritant next to the eye and may cause more damage. You should wash out your eye right away while you wait for medical help.
MeSH definition (Eye Injuries): Damage or trauma inflicted to the eye by external means. The concept includes both surface injuries and intraocular injuries.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Corneal Disorders, Eye Cancer, Eye Care, Eye Diseases, Eye Infections, Eye Movement Disorders, Eyelid Disorders, Optic Nerve Disorders, Refractive Errors, Retinal Disorders, Tears, Vision Impairment and Blindness$rounds_kb$)
