insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$foot-injuries-and-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-508$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Foot Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Foot Injuries and Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad anatomic umbrella covering many distinct injuries and conditions; no single diagnosis or presentation.", "kind": "other", "category": "foot disorders (umbrella)", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Each of your feet has 26 bones, 33 joints, and more than 100 tendons, muscles, and ligaments. No wonder a lot of things can go wrong. Here are a few common problems:
- Bunions - hard, painful bumps on the big toe joint
- Corns and calluses - thickened skin from friction or pressure
- Plantar warts - warts on the soles of your feet
- Fallen arches - also called flat feet
Ill-fitting shoes often cause these problems. Aging and being overweight also increase your chances of having foot problems.
MeSH definition (Foot Diseases): Anatomical and functional disorders affecting the foot.
MeSH definition (Foot Injuries): General or unspecified injuries involving the foot.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Ankle Injuries and Disorders, Bone Diseases, Breast Diseases, Cartilage Disorders, Dandruff, Cradle Cap, and Other Scalp Conditions, Hair Problems, Itching, Jaw Injuries and Disorders, Joint Disorders, Knee Injuries and Disorders, Leg Injuries and Disorders, Muscle Disorders, Nail Diseases, Rashes, Rosacea$rounds_kb$)
