insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$gaucher-disease$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1523$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Gaucher Disease$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$blood$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Gaucher Disease", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Lysosomal storage disorder with hepatosplenomegaly, cytopenias and bone findings; diagnosis via enzyme assay and genetics.", "kind": "disease", "category": "lysosomal storage disorder", "organ_systems": ["blood", "musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["pediatrics", "neurology"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Gaucher disease is a rare, inherited disorder. It is a type of lipid metabolism disorder. If you have it, you do not have enough of an enzyme called glucocerebrosidase. This causes too much of a fatty substance to build up in your spleen, liver, lungs, bones and, sometimes, your brain. This prevents these organs from working properly.
There are three types:
- Type 1, the most common form, causes liver and spleen enlargement, bone pain and fractures (broken bones), and, sometimes, lung and kidney problems. It does not affect the brain. It can occur at any age.
- Type 2, which causes severe brain damage, appears in infants. Most children who have it die by age 2.
- In type 3, there may be liver and spleen enlargement. The brain is gradually affected. It usually starts in childhood or adolescence.
Gaucher disease has no cure. Treatment options for types 1 and 3 include medicine and enzyme replacement therapy, which is usually very effective. There is no good treatment for the brain damage of types 2 and 3.
NIH: National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke
MeSH definition (Gaucher Disease): An autosomal recessive disorder caused by a deficiency of acid beta-glucosidase (GLUCOSYLCERAMIDASE) leading to intralysosomal accumulation of glycosylceramide mainly in cells of the MONONUCLEAR PHAGOCYTE SYSTEM. The characteristic Gaucher cells, glycosphingolipid-filled HISTIOCYTES, displace normal cells in BONE MARROW and visceral organs causing skeletal deterioration, hepatosplenomegaly, and organ dysfunction. There are several subtypes based on the presence and severity of neurological involvement.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Leukodystrophies$rounds_kb$)
