insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$hair-problems$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-531$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Hair Problems$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Hair Problems", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of diseases affecting hair growth rather than a specific diagnosis a student can reach by interview and workup.", "kind": "other", "category": "dermatologic category", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": [], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The average person has 5 million hairs. Hair grows all over your body except on your lips, palms, and the soles of your feet. It takes about a month for healthy hair to grow half an inch. Most hairs grow for up to six years and then fall out. New hairs grow in their place.
Hair helps keep you warm. It also protects your eyes, ears and nose from small particles in the air. Common problem with the hair and scalp include hair loss, infections, and flaking.
MeSH definition (Hair Diseases): Diseases affecting the orderly growth and persistence of hair.
MeSH definition (Dandruff): Excessive shedding of dry scaly material from the scalp in humans.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Breast Diseases, Dandruff, Cradle Cap, and Other Scalp Conditions, Eczema, Foot Injuries and Disorders, Itching, Nail Diseases, Rashes, Rosacea, Scleroderma, Skin Cancer, Skin Infections, Skin Pigmentation Disorders$rounds_kb$)
