insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$hantavirus-infections$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-3217$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Hantavirus Infections$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$respiratory$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$blood$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$renal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Hantavirus Infections", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Hantavirus pulmonary syndrome presents with fever, myalgias and rapidly progressive respiratory failure after rodent exposure; reachable by history and testing.", "kind": "disease", "category": "viral zoonotic infection", "organ_systems": ["respiratory", "blood", "renal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["inpatient", "icu", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Hantavirus pulmonary syndrome (HPS) is a rare viral infection caused by several strains of the hantavirus. It is spread by mice and rats. They shed the virus in their urine, droppings, and saliva. Tiny droplets with the virus can enter the air. You can get the disease if you breathe infected air or come into contact with rodents or their urine or droppings.
Most of the time, you can't get the virus from another person. But one strain of the virus found in South America, called the Andes virus, spreads through close contact with someone who has the virus.
Early symptoms of HPS include:
- Fatigue
- Fever
- Muscle aches, especially in the thighs, hips, and back
- Headaches
- Chills
- Dizziness
- Nausea, vomiting, diarrhea or abdominal (belly) pain
Later symptoms include coughing and shortness of breath.
Controlling rodents in and around your house is the best way to prevent infection. If you have been around rodents and have symptoms of fever, deep muscle aches, and severe shortness of breath, see your health care provider immediately. Early treatment is important.
There is no specific treatment, cure, or vaccine for HPS.
Centers for Disease Control and Prevention
MeSH definition (Hantavirus Infections): Infections with viruses of the genus ORTHOHANTAVIRUS. This is associated with at least four clinical syndromes: HEMORRHAGIC FEVER WITH RENAL SYNDROME caused by viruses of the Hantaan group; a milder form of HFRS caused by SEOUL VIRUS; nephropathia epidemica caused by PUUMALA VIRUS; and HANTAVIRUS PULMONARY SYNDROME caused by SIN NOMBRE VIRUS.
Also called: HPS, Hanta virus$rounds_kb$)
