insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$herpes-simplex$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-286$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Herpes Simplex$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$very_common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$reproductive$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Herpes Simplex", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Painful vesicular lesions with characteristic history; diagnosis by exam and testing, with counseling and management implications.", "kind": "disease", "category": "viral infection", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal", "reproductive"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["obgyn", "internalMedicine", "pediatrics"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Herpes is an infection that is caused by a herpes simplex virus (HSV). Oral herpes causes cold sores around the mouth or face. Genital herpes affects the genitals, buttocks or anal area. Genital herpes is a sexually transmitted infection (STI). It affects the genitals, buttocks or anal area. Other herpes infections can affect the eyes, skin, or other parts of the body. The virus can be dangerous in newborn babies or in people with weak immune systems.
There are two types of HSV:
- HSV type 1 most commonly causes cold sores. It can also cause genital herpes.
- HSV type 2 is the usual cause of genital herpes, but it also can infect the mouth.
HSV spreads through direct contact. Some people have no symptoms. Others get sores near the area where the virus has entered the body. They turn into blisters, become itchy and painful, and then heal.
Most people have outbreaks several times a year. Over time, you get them less often. Medicines to help your body fight the virus can help lessen symptoms and decrease outbreaks.
MeSH definition (Herpes Simplex): A group of acute infections caused by herpes simplex virus type 1 or type 2 that is characterized by the development of one or more small fluid-filled vesicles with a raised erythematous base on the skin or mucous membrane. It occurs as a primary infection or recurs due to a reactivation of a latent infection. (Dorland, 27th ed.)
Also called: HSV
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Bell's Palsy, Cytomegalovirus Infections, Fifth Disease, Kaposi Sarcoma, Warts$rounds_kb$)
