MeSH definition (Infectious Mononucleosis): A common, acute infection usually caused by the Epstein-Barr virus (HERPESVIRUS 4, HUMAN). There is an increase in mononuclear white blood cells and other atypical lymphocytes, generalized lymphadenopathy, splenomegaly, and occasionally hepatomegaly with hepatitis.
Also called: Glandular fever, Kissing disease, Mono, Mononucleosis
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Acute Lymphocytic Leukemia, Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia, Eosinophilic Disorders, Lymphoma, Multiple Myeloma, Sarcoidosis$rounds_kb$)
