insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$intestinal-cancer$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-3652$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Intestinal Cancer$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Intestinal Cancer", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Small bowel malignancy presenting with obstruction, bleeding or weight loss; a real diagnosis reachable by imaging and endoscopy, though rare.", "kind": "disease", "category": "malignancy", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["inpatient", "clinic"], "is_cancer": true}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your small intestine is part of your digestive system. It is a long tube that connects your stomach to your large intestine. Intestinal cancer is rare, but eating a high-fat diet or having Crohn's disease, celiac disease, or a history of colonic polyps can increase your risk.
Possible signs of small intestine cancer include:
- Abdominal pain
- Weight loss for no reason
- Blood in the stool
- A lump in the abdomen
Imaging tests that create pictures of the small intestine and the area around it can help diagnose intestinal cancer and show whether it has spread.
Surgery is the most common treatment. Additional options include chemotherapy, radiation therapy, or a combination.
NIH: National Cancer Institute
MeSH definition (Ileal Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer in the ILEUM region of the small intestine (INTESTINE, SMALL).
MeSH definition (Jejunal Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer in the JEJUNUM region of the small intestine (INTESTINE, SMALL).
MeSH definition (Duodenal Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer of the DUODENUM.
Also called: Duodenal cancer, Ileal cancer, Jejunal cancer, Small intestine cancer
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Colorectal Cancer, Peptic Ulcer$rounds_kb$)
