insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$intestinal-obstruction$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5275$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Intestinal Obstruction$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Intestinal Obstruction", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Classic acute abdomen with vomiting, distension and absent flatus; clear diagnosis via exam and imaging, with important surgical decision-making.", "kind": "disease", "category": "acute surgical abdomen", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "internalMedicine", "pediatrics"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["emergency", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$An intestinal obstruction occurs when food or stool cannot move through the intestines. The obstruction can be complete or partial. There are many causes. The most common are adhesions, hernias, cancers, and certain medicines.
Symptoms include:
- Severe abdominal pain or cramping
- Vomiting
- Bloating
- Loud bowel sounds
- Swelling of the abdomen
- Inability to pass gas
- Constipation
A complete intestinal obstruction is a medical emergency. It often requires surgery.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Intestinal Obstruction): Any impairment, arrest, or reversal of the normal flow of INTESTINAL CONTENTS toward the ANAL CANAL.
Also called: Bowel obstruction, Intestinal volvulus, Paralytic ileus
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Colonic Diseases, Malabsorption Syndromes, Rectal Disorders, Small Intestine Disorders$rounds_kb$)
