insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$liver-cancer$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-309$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Liver Cancer$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Liver Cancer", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Hepatocellular carcinoma typically arising in cirrhosis; reachable by history, exam, imaging and AFP, with clear risk factors.", "kind": "disease", "category": "gastrointestinal malignancy", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["surgery", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": true}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your liver is the largest organ inside your body. It helps your body digest food, store energy, and remove poisons. Primary liver cancer starts in the liver. Metastatic liver cancer starts somewhere else and spreads to your liver.
Risk factors for primary liver cancer include :
- Having hepatitis B or C
- Heavy alcohol use
- Having cirrhosis, or scarring of the liver
- Having hemochromatosis, an iron storage disease
- Obesity and diabetes
Symptoms can include a lump or pain on the right side of your abdomen and yellowing of the skin. However, you may not have symptoms until the cancer is advanced. This makes it harder to treat. Doctors use tests that examine the liver and the blood to diagnose liver cancer. Treatment options include surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, or liver transplantation.
NIH: National Cancer Institute
MeSH definition (Liver Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer of the LIVER.
Also called: Hepatocellular carcinoma
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency, Cirrhosis, Drug Reactions, Hepatitis, Ovarian Cancer, Pancreatic Cancer, Steatotic Liver Disease, Wilson Disease$rounds_kb$)
