insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$malabsorption-syndromes$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5459$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Malabsorption Syndromes$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Malabsorption Syndromes", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Umbrella term for many distinct causes of malabsorption rather than a single diagnosis; better represented by specific entities like celiac disease.", "kind": "other", "category": "gastrointestinal absorption disorder", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": [], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your small intestine does most of the digesting of the foods you eat. If you have a malabsorption syndrome, your small intestine cannot absorb nutrients from foods.
Causes of malabsorption syndromes include:
- Celiac disease
- Lactose intolerance
- Short bowel syndrome. This happens after surgery to remove half or more of the small intestine. You might need the surgery if you have a problem with the small intestine from a disease, injury, or birth defect.
- Whipple disease, a rare bacterial infection
- Genetic diseases
- Certain medicines
Symptoms of different malabsorption syndromes can vary. They often include chronic diarrhea, abnormal stools, weight loss, and gas. Your doctor may use lab, imaging, or other tests to make a diagnosis.
Treatment of malabsorption syndromes depends on the cause.
MeSH definition (Malabsorption Syndromes): General term for a group of MALNUTRITION syndromes caused by failure of normal INTESTINAL ABSORPTION of nutrients.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Colonic Diseases, Fluid and Electrolyte Balance, Intestinal Obstruction, Lipid Metabolism Disorders, Metabolic Syndrome, Mitochondrial Diseases, Porphyria, Rectal Disorders, Small Intestine Disorders$rounds_kb$)
