insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$muscle-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-510$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Muscle Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Muscle Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of myopathies, not a single diagnosis; specific entities like dermatomyositis or muscular dystrophy are case-suitable.", "kind": "other", "category": "neuromuscular", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal", "nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "neurology", "secondary_clerkships": [], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your muscles help you move and help your body work. Different types of muscles have different jobs. There are many problems that can affect muscles. Muscle disorders can cause weakness, pain or even paralysis.
Causes of muscle disorders include:
- Injury or overuse, such as sprains or strains, cramps or tendinitis
- A genetic disorder, such as muscular dystrophy
- Some cancers
- Inflammation, such as myositis
- Diseases of nerves that affect muscles
- Infections
- Certain medicines
Sometimes the cause of muscle disorders is unknown.
MeSH definition (Muscular Diseases): Acquired, familial, and congenital disorders of SKELETAL MUSCLE and SMOOTH MUSCLE.
Also called: Myopathy
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Bone Diseases, Cartilage Disorders, Foot Injuries and Disorders, Jaw Injuries and Disorders, Joint Disorders, Myalgic Encephalomyelitis/Chronic Fatigue Syndrome, Peripheral Nerve Disorders, Polio and Post-Polio Syndrome$rounds_kb$)
