insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$nail-diseases$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-532$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Nail Diseases$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Nail Diseases", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of nail findings rather than a single diagnosis; no coherent patient presentation to work up.", "kind": "disease", "category": "dermatologic disorder", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": [], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your toenails and fingernails protect the tissues of your toes and fingers. They are made up of layers of a hardened protein called keratin, which is also in your hair and skin. The health of your nails can be a clue to your overall health. Healthy nails are usually smooth and consistent in color. Specific types of nail discoloration and changes in growth rate can be signs of lung, heart, kidney, and liver diseases, as well as diabetes and anemia. White spots and vertical ridges are harmless.
Nail problems that sometimes require treatment include:
- Bacterial and fungal infections
- Ingrown nails
- Tumors
- Warts
Keeping your nails clean, dry, and trimmed can help you avoid some problems. Do not remove the cuticle, which can cause infection.
MeSH definition (Nail Diseases): Diseases of the nail plate and tissues surrounding it. The concept is limited to primates.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Breast Diseases, Dandruff, Cradle Cap, and Other Scalp Conditions, Foot Injuries and Disorders, Hair Problems, Itching, Rashes, Rosacea, Scleroderma, Skin Cancer, Skin Infections, Skin Pigmentation Disorders$rounds_kb$)
