MeSH definition (Nutritional Physiological Phenomena): The processes and properties of living organisms by which they take in and balance the use of nutritive materials for energy, heat production, or building material for the growth, maintenance, or repair of tissues and the nutritive properties of FOOD.
MeSH definition (Nutrition Disorders): Disorders caused by nutritional imbalance, either overnutrition or undernutrition.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Metabolic Disorders, Nutrition for Older Adults$rounds_kb$)
