MeSH definition (Peritoneal Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer of the PERITONEUM.
MeSH definition (Fallopian Tube Neoplasms): Benign or malignant neoplasms of the FALLOPIAN TUBES. They are uncommon. If they develop, they may be located in the wall or within the lumen as a growth attached to the wall by a stalk.
MeSH definition (Ovarian Neoplasms): Tumors or cancer of the OVARY. These neoplasms can be benign or malignant. They are classified according to the tissue of origin, such as the surface EPITHELIUM, the stromal endocrine cells, and the totipotent GERM CELLS.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Adrenal Gland Cancer, Liver Cancer, Ovarian Cysts, Pancreatic Cancer, Pituitary Tumors, Primary Ovarian Insufficiency, Testicular Cancer, Thyroid Cancer, Uterine Cancer, Uterine Fibroids, Vaginal Cancer, Vulvar Cancer$rounds_kb$)
