insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$pituitary-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-362$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Pituitary Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$endocrine$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Pituitary Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category covering hypopituitarism, diabetes insipidus and others; too heterogeneous to be a single interviewable case.", "kind": "disease", "category": "endocrine", "organ_systems": ["endocrine"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Your pituitary gland is a pea-sized gland at the base of your brain. The pituitary is the "master control gland" - it makes hormones that affect growth and the functions of other glands in the body.
With pituitary disorders, you often have too much or too little of one of your hormones. Injuries can cause pituitary disorders, but the most common cause is a pituitary tumor.
MeSH definition (Pituitary Diseases): Disorders involving either the ADENOHYPOPHYSIS or the NEUROHYPOPHYSIS. These diseases usually manifest as hypersecretion or hyposecretion of PITUITARY HORMONES. Neoplastic pituitary masses can also cause compression of the OPTIC CHIASM and other adjacent structures.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Adrenal Gland Disorders, Diabetes, Diabetes in Children and Teens, Diabetic Heart Disease, Dwarfism, Endocrine Diseases, Parathyroid Disorders, Thyroid Diseases$rounds_kb$)
