MeSH definition (Prediabetic State): The time period before the development of symptomatic diabetes. For example, certain risk factors can be observed in subjects who subsequently develop INSULIN RESISTANCE as in type 2 diabetes (DIABETES MELLITUS, TYPE 2).
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Diabetes Complications, Diabetes Type 1, Diabetes Type 2, How to Prevent Diabetes$rounds_kb$)
