insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$rectal-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5870$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Rectal Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Rectal Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "A broad category of anorectal conditions, not a single diagnosis; specific entities like hemorrhoids or anal fissure would be suitable.", "kind": "other", "category": "category", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The rectum is the lower part of your large intestine where your body stores stool. Problems with the rectum are common. They include hemorrhoids, abscesses, incontinence and cancer.
Many people are embarrassed to talk about rectal troubles. But seeing your doctor about problems in this area is important. This is especially true if you have pain or bleeding. Treatments vary depending on the particular problem.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Rectal Diseases): Pathological developments in the RECTUM region of the large intestine (INTESTINE, LARGE).
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Colonic Diseases, Intestinal Obstruction, Malabsorption Syndromes, Small Intestine Disorders$rounds_kb$)
