insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$sexual-problems-in-men$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-5571$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Sexual Problems in Men$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$reproductive$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Sexual Problems in Men", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category (erectile dysfunction, premature ejaculation, low libido) rather than a single diagnosis; better as a specific entity.", "kind": "other", "category": "broad category", "organ_systems": ["reproductive"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Many men have sexual problems. They become more common as men age. Problems can include:
- Erectile dysfunction
- Reduced or lost interest in sex
- Problems with ejaculation
- Low testosterone
Stress, illness, medicines, or emotional problems may also be factors. Occasional problems with sexual function are common. If problems last more than a few months or cause distress for you or your partner, you should see your health care provider.
MeSH definition (Sexual Dysfunction, Physiological): Physiological disturbances in normal sexual performance in either the male or the female.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Infertility, Sexually Transmitted Infections$rounds_kb$)
