insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$sexual-problems-in-women$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1423$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Sexual Problems in Women$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$reproductive$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Sexual Problems in Women", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Heterogeneous category of female sexual dysfunction; too broad to be one interviewable diagnosis.", "kind": "other", "category": "broad category", "organ_systems": ["reproductive"], "primary_clerkship": "obgyn", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$There are many problems that can keep a woman from enjoying sex. They include:
- Lack of sexual desire
- Inability to become aroused
- Lack of orgasm, or sexual climax
- Painful intercourse
These problems may have physical or psychological causes. Physical causes may include conditions like diabetes, heart disease, nerve disorders, or hormone problems. Some drugs can also affect desire and function. Psychological causes may include work-related stress and anxiety. They may also include depression or concerns about marriage or relationship problems. For some women, the problem results from past sexual trauma.
Occasional problems with sexual function are common. If problems last more than a few months or cause distress for you or your partner, you should see your health care provider.
MeSH definition (Vaginismus): Recurrent or persistent involuntary SPASM of the outer muscles of the VAGINA, occurring during vaginal penetration.
MeSH definition (Dyspareunia): Recurrent genital pain occurring during, before, or after SEXUAL INTERCOURSE in either the male or the female.
MeSH definition (Sexual Dysfunctions, Psychological): Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Anxiety, Child Mental Health, Drug Use and Addiction, Drugs and Young People, Eating Disorders, Endometriosis, Erectile Dysfunction, Female Infertility, Genital Herpes, Male Infertility, Mental Disorders, Mood Disorders, Penis Disorders, Personality Disorders, Pregnancy and Substance Use$rounds_kb$)
