insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$swallowing-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1309$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Swallowing Disorders$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Swallowing Disorders", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Dysphagia is a common presenting complaint with a broad differential (neurologic vs mechanical) reachable by history, exam and testing.", "kind": "symptom", "category": "esophageal and oropharyngeal dysfunction", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal", "nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology", "familyMedicine", "surgery"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$If you have a swallowing disorder, you may have difficulty or pain when swallowing. Some people cannot swallow at all. Others may have trouble swallowing liquids, foods, or saliva. This makes it hard to eat. Often, it can be difficult to take in enough calories and fluids to nourish your body.
Anyone can have a swallowing disorder, but it is more common in older adults. It often happens because of other conditions, including:
- Nervous system disorders, such as Parkinson's disease and cerebral palsy
- Problems with your esophagus, including GERD (gastroesophageal reflux disease)
- Stroke
- Head or spinal cord injury
- Cancer of the head, neck, or esophagus
Medicines can help some people, while others may need surgery. Swallowing treatment with a speech-language pathologist can help. You may find it helpful to change your diet or hold your head or neck in a certain way when you eat. In very serious cases, people may need feeding tubes.
NIH: National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders
MeSH definition (Deglutition Disorders): Difficulty in SWALLOWING which may result from neuromuscular disorder or mechanical obstruction. Dysphagia is classified into two distinct types: oropharyngeal dysphagia due to malfunction of the PHARYNX and UPPER ESOPHAGEAL SPHINCTER; and esophageal dysphagia due to malfunction of the ESOPHAGUS.
Also called: Dysphagia
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Esophageal Cancer, Sore Throat, Throat Cancer$rounds_kb$)
