insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$tailbone-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1448$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Tailbone Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Tailbone Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad anatomic category rather than a specific diagnosis; coccydynia is a symptom and the grouping lacks a coherent case-defining presentation.", "kind": "other", "category": "musculoskeletal pain", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$The tailbone is the small bone at the bottom of your backbone, or spine. Tailbone disorders include tailbone injuries, pain, infections, cysts and tumors. You rarely break your tailbone. Instead, most injuries cause bruises or pulled ligaments. A backward fall onto a hard surface, such as slipping on ice, is the most common cause of such injuries. Symptoms of various tailbone disorders include pain in the tailbone area, pain upon sitting, pain or numbness in the arms or legs due to pressure on nerves in the tailbone area, and a mass or growth you can see or feel.
MeSH definition (Coccyx): The last bone in the VERTEBRAL COLUMN in tailless primates considered to be a vestigial tail-bone consisting of three to five fused VERTEBRAE.
MeSH definition (Spinal Diseases): Diseases involving the SPINE.
Also called: Coccyx disorders
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Bone Cancer, Bone Infections, Neck Injuries and Disorders, Osteonecrosis, Paget's Disease of Bone, Spine Injuries and Disorders$rounds_kb$)
