insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$taste-and-smell-disorders$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-430$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Taste and Smell Disorders$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Taste and Smell Disorders", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of sensory dysfunction rather than a single diagnosis; workup is diffuse and presentation overlaps many causes.", "kind": "symptom", "category": "sensory dysfunction", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "neurology", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Our senses of taste and smell give us great pleasure. Taste helps us enjoy food and beverages. Smell lets us enjoy the scents and fragrances like roses or coffee. Taste and smell also protect us, letting us know when food has gone bad or when there is a gas leak. They make us want to eat, ensuring we get the nutrition we need.
People with taste disorders may taste things that aren't there, may not be able to tell the difference in tastes, or can't taste at all. People with smell disorders may lose their sense of smell, or things may smell different. A smell they once enjoyed may now smell bad to them.
Many illnesses and injuries can cause taste and smell disorders, including colds and head injuries. Some drugs can also affect taste and smell. Most people lose some ability to taste and smell as they get older. Treatment varies, depending on the problem and its cause.
NIH: National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders
MeSH definition (Taste Disorders): Conditions characterized by an alteration in gustatory function or perception. Taste disorders are frequently associated with OLFACTION DISORDERS. Additional potential etiologies include METABOLIC DISEASES; DRUG TOXICITY; and taste pathway disorders (e.g., TASTE BUD diseases; FACIAL NERVE DISEASES; GLOSSOPHARYNGEAL NERVE DISEASES; and BRAIN STEM diseases).
MeSH definition (Taste Perception): The process by which the nature and meaning of gustatory stimuli are recognized and interpreted by the brain. The five basic classes of taste perception are salty, sweet, bitter, sour and umami.
MeSH definition (Olfaction Disorders): Impaired ability to smell. This may be caused by OLFACTORY NERVE DISEASES; PARANASAL SINUS DISEASES; viral RESPIRATORY TRACT INFECTIONS; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; SMOKING; and other conditions.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Dizziness and Vertigo, Hearing Disorders and Deafness, Hearing Problems in Children, Pain, Vision Impairment and Blindness$rounds_kb$)
