insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$tuberous-sclerosis$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1375$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Tuberous Sclerosis$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Tuberous Sclerosis", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Multisystem neurocutaneous disorder with skin findings, seizures and developmental delay; diagnosis is clinical with imaging and genetic confirmation.", "kind": "disease", "category": "neurocutaneous syndrome", "organ_systems": ["nervous", "musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "pediatrics", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["clinic", "pediatric_clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Tuberous sclerosis is a rare genetic disease that causes benign tumors to grow in the brain and other organs. Symptoms vary, depending on where the tumors grow. They could include:
- Skin problems, such as light patches and thickened skin
- Seizures
- Behavior problems
- Intellectual disabilities
- Kidney problems
Some people have signs of tuberous sclerosis at birth. In others it can take time for the symptoms to develop. The disease can be mild, or it can cause severe disabilities. In rare cases, tumors in vital organs or other symptoms can be life-threatening.
Tuberous sclerosis has no cure, but treatments can help symptoms. Options include medicines, educational and occupational therapy, surgery, or surgery to treat specific complications.
NIH: National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke
MeSH definition (Tuberous Sclerosis): Autosomal dominant neurocutaneous syndrome classically characterized by MENTAL RETARDATION; EPILEPSY; and skin lesions (e.g., adenoma sebaceum and hypomelanotic macules). There is, however, considerable heterogeneity in the neurologic manifestations. It is also associated with cortical tuber and HAMARTOMAS formation throughout the body, especially the heart, kidneys, and eyes. Mutations in two loci TSC1 and TSC2 that encode hamartin and tuberin, respectively, are associated with the disease.
Also called: TSC, Tuberous sclerosis complex
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Ataxia Telangiectasia, Breast Cancer, Huntington's Disease, Leukodystrophies, Neurofibromatosis, Tourette Syndrome, Von Hippel-Lindau Disease, Wilms Tumor, Wilson Disease$rounds_kb$)
