insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$vaginal-diseases$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-451$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Vaginal Diseases$rounds_kb$, false, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$reproductive$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Vaginal Diseases", "case_suitable": false, "reason": "Broad category of vaginal pathology rather than a single diagnosis; no single patient presentation.", "kind": "other", "category": "gynecologic disorders", "organ_systems": ["reproductive"], "primary_clerkship": "obgyn", "secondary_clerkships": ["familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["clinic"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Vaginal problems are some of the most common reasons women go to the doctor. They may have symptoms such as:
- Itching
- Burning
- Pain
- Abnormal bleeding
- Discharge
One common problem is vaginitis, an inflammation of the vagina. Other problems that affect the vagina include sexually transmitted infections (STIs), vaginal cancer, and vulvar cancer. Treatment of vaginal problems depends on the cause.
MeSH definition (Vaginal Diseases): Pathological processes of the VAGINA.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Endometriosis, Female Infertility, Genital Herpes, Sexual Problems in Women, Uterine Diseases, Vulvar Disorders$rounds_kb$)
