insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$wilson-disease$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$mplus-1691$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Wilson Disease$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$gastrointestinal$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Wilson Disease", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Rare inherited copper metabolism disorder with hepatic and neuropsychiatric findings; good for multisystem differential reasoning.", "kind": "disease", "category": "inherited metabolic disorder", "organ_systems": ["gastrointestinal", "nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology", "pediatrics", "psychiatry"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$Wilson disease is a rare inherited disorder that prevents your body from getting rid of extra copper. You need a small amount of copper from food to stay healthy. Too much copper is poisonous.
Normally, your liver releases extra copper into bile, a digestive fluid. With Wilson disease, the copper builds up in your liver, and it releases the copper directly into your bloodstream. This can cause damage to your brain, kidneys, and eyes.
Wilson disease is present at birth, but symptoms usually start between ages 5 and 35. It first attacks the liver, the central nervous system or both. The most characteristic sign is a rusty brown ring around the cornea of the eye. A physical exam and laboratory tests can diagnose it.
Treatment is with drugs to remove the extra copper from your body. You need to take medicine and follow a low-copper diet for the rest of your life. Don't eat shellfish or liver, as these foods may contain high levels of copper. At the beginning of treatment, you'll also need to avoid chocolate, mushrooms, and nuts. Have your drinking water checked for copper content and don't take multivitamins that contain copper.
With early detection and proper treatment, you can enjoy good health.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Hepatolenticular Degeneration): A rare autosomal recessive disease characterized by the deposition of copper in the BRAIN; LIVER; CORNEA; and other organs. It is caused by defects in the ATP7B gene encoding copper-transporting ATPase 2 (EC 3.6.3.4), also known as the Wilson disease protein. The overload of copper inevitably leads to progressive liver and neurological dysfunction such as LIVER CIRRHOSIS; TREMOR; ATAXIA and intellectual deterioration. Hepatic dysfunction may precede neurologic dysfunction by several years.
Also called: Copper storage disease, Hepatolenticular degeneration
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency, Cirrhosis, Drug Reactions, Hemochromatosis, Hepatitis, Huntington's Disease, Leukodystrophies, Liver Cancer, Neurofibromatosis, Phenylketonuria, Progressive Supranuclear Palsy, Steatotic Liver Disease, Tourette Syndrome, Tuberous Sclerosis$rounds_kb$)
