insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$compartment-syndrome$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$ct-19390$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Compartment syndrome$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Compartment syndrome", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Pain out of proportion after trauma or casting is a classic diagnosis made from history, exam and compartment pressure measurement, with a clear time-critical workup.", "kind": "disease", "category": "orthopedic emergency", "organ_systems": ["musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "surgery", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["emergency", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Compartment Syndromes): Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the BLOOD CIRCULATION and function of tissue within that space. Some of the causes of increased pressure are TRAUMA, tight dressings, HEMORRHAGE, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression (NERVE COMPRESSION SYNDROMES); PARALYSIS; and ISCHEMIC CONTRACTURE. FASCIOTOMY is often used to decompress increased pressure and eliminate pain associated with compartment syndromes.
Also called: elevated compartment pressure
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Aneurysms, Arteriovenous Malformations, Fibromyalgia, Hemorrhoids, High Blood Pressure, How to Prevent High Blood Pressure, Low Blood Pressure, Muscle Cramps, Myalgic Encephalomyelitis/Chronic Fatigue Syndrome, Myositis, Polymyalgia Rheumatica, Tendinitis, Thoracic Outlet Syndrome, Varicose Veins, Vasculitis$rounds_kb$)
