MeSH definition (Spermatic Cord Torsion): The twisting of the SPERMATIC CORD due to an anatomical abnormality that left the TESTIS mobile and dangling in the SCROTUM. The initial effect of testicular torsion is obstruction of venous return. Depending on the duration and degree of cord rotation, testicular symptoms range from EDEMA to interrupted arterial flow and testicular pain. If blood flow to testis is absent for 4 to 6 h, SPERMATOGENESIS may be permanently lost.
Also called: torsion of testis
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Erectile Dysfunction, Genital Herpes, Male Infertility, Penis Disorders, Prostate Diseases, Sexual Problems in Women, Testicular Disorders$rounds_kb$)
