insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$febrile-seizure$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$ct-6697$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Febrile seizure$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Febrile seizure", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Young child with a seizure during fever is a common pediatric presentation where the diagnosis is reached by history and exam while excluding meningitis and other causes.", "kind": "disease", "category": "seizure disorder", "organ_systems": ["nervous"], "primary_clerkship": "pediatrics", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "familyMedicine", "neurology"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["emergency", "pediatric_clinic", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Seizures, Febrile): Seizures that occur during a febrile episode. It is a common condition, affecting 2-5% of children aged 3 months to five years. An autosomal dominant pattern of inheritance has been identified in some families. The majority are simple febrile seizures (generally defined as generalized onset, single seizures with a duration of less than 30 minutes). Complex febrile seizures are characterized by focal onset, duration greater than 30 minutes, and/or more than one seizure in a 24 hour period. The likelihood of developing epilepsy (i.e., a nonfebrile seizure disorder) following simple febrile seizures is low. Complex febrile seizures are associated with a moderately increased incidence of epilepsy. (From Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, p784)
Also called: Seizure - febrile, seizure (febrile) szs$rounds_kb$)
