insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$postpartum-hemorrhage$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$core-postpartum-hemorrhage$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Postpartum hemorrhage$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$reproductive$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$blood$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Postpartum hemorrhage", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Acute obstetric emergency with a clear presentation (heavy bleeding after delivery) and a differential of uterine atony, retained placenta, lacerations and coagulopathy that students can work through.", "kind": "disease", "category": "obstetric emergency", "organ_systems": ["reproductive", "blood"], "primary_clerkship": "obgyn", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "familyMedicine"], "commonness": "common", "settings": ["labor_delivery", "emergency", "icu"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Postpartum Hemorrhage): Excess blood loss from uterine bleeding associated with OBSTETRIC LABOR or CHILDBIRTH. It is defined as blood loss greater than 500 ml or of the amount that adversely affects the maternal physiology, such as BLOOD PRESSURE and HEMATOCRIT. Postpartum hemorrhage is divided into two categories, immediate (within first 24 hours after birth) or delayed (after 24 hours postpartum).
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Breast Diseases, Postpartum Depression, Preterm Labor$rounds_kb$)
