insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$neuroleptic-malignant-syndrome$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$ct-8527$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Neuroleptic malignant syndrome$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$rare$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$behavioral$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Neuroleptic malignant syndrome", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Rare but classic drug-induced syndrome with fever, rigidity and autonomic instability; a good differential against serotonin syndrome and catatonia.", "kind": "disease", "category": "adverse drug reaction", "organ_systems": ["nervous", "behavioral"], "primary_clerkship": "psychiatry", "secondary_clerkships": ["neurology", "emergency", "internalMedicine"], "commonness": "rare", "settings": ["inpatient", "emergency", "icu", "psychiatric"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome): A potentially fatal syndrome associated primarily with the use of neuroleptic agents (see ANTIPSYCHOTIC AGENTS) which are in turn associated with dopaminergic receptor blockade (see RECEPTORS, DOPAMINE) in the BASAL GANGLIA and HYPOTHALAMUS, and sympathetic dysregulation. Clinical features include diffuse MUSCLE RIGIDITY; TREMOR; high FEVER; diaphoresis; labile blood pressure; cognitive dysfunction; and autonomic disturbances. Serum CPK level elevation and a leukocytosis may also be present. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1199; Psychiatr Serv 1998 Sep;49(9):1163-72)
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Botulism, Huntington's Disease, Progressive Supranuclear Palsy, Tourette Syndrome, Wilson Disease$rounds_kb$)
