insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$serotonin-syndrome$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$core-serotonin-syndrome$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Serotonin syndrome$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$psychiatry$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$behavioral$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Serotonin syndrome", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Drug-induced toxidrome with altered mental status, autonomic findings and clonus; students can identify it from medication history and exam and contrast it with NMS.", "kind": "disease", "category": "adverse drug reaction", "organ_systems": ["nervous", "behavioral"], "primary_clerkship": "emergency", "secondary_clerkships": ["psychiatry", "internalMedicine", "neurology"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["emergency", "inpatient", "icu"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Serotonin Syndrome): An adverse drug interaction characterized by altered mental status, autonomic dysfunction, and neuromuscular abnormalities. It is most frequently caused by use of both serotonin reuptake inhibitors and monoamine oxidase inhibitors, leading to excess serotonin availability in the CNS at the serotonin 1A receptor.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Drug Reactions$rounds_kb$)
