insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$urinary-tract-infection$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$ct-2281$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Urinary tract infection$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$very_common$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pediatrics$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$obgyn$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$renal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Urinary tract infection", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Extremely common presentation with dysuria and frequency; diagnosis is clinical with urinalysis and culture, and the differential includes vaginitis and urethritis.", "kind": "disease", "category": "infection", "organ_systems": ["renal"], "primary_clerkship": "familyMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["internalMedicine", "emergency", "pediatrics", "obgyn"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$(Broader MedlinePlus topic: Urinary Tract Infections) The urinary system is the body's drainage system for removing wastes and extra water. It includes two kidneys, two ureters, a bladder, and a urethra. Urinary tract infections (UTIs) are the second most common type of infection in the body.
You may have a UTI if you notice:
- Pain or burning when you urinate
- Fever, tiredness, or shakiness
- An urge to urinate often
- Pressure in your lower belly
- Urine that smells bad or looks cloudy or reddish
- Pain in your back or side below the ribs
People of any age or sex can get UTIs. But about four times as many women get UTIs as men. You're also at higher risk if you have diabetes, need a tube to drain your bladder, or have a spinal cord injury.
If you think you have a UTI it is important to see your doctor. Your doctor can tell if you have a UTI with a urine test. Treatment is with antibiotics.
NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases
MeSH definition (Urinary Tract Infections): Inflammatory responses of the epithelium of the URINARY TRACT to microbial invasions. They are often bacterial infections with associated BACTERIURIA and PYURIA.
Also called: UTI, bladder infection, urinar urinary tract infection
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Animal Diseases and Your Health, Bladder Diseases, Bone Infections, Eye Infections, Infections and Pregnancy, Infectious Arthritis, Infectious Diseases, Kidney Diseases, Parasitic Diseases, Sepsis, Sexually Transmitted Infections, Skin Infections, Ureteral Disorders, Urethral Disorders, Urinary Tract Infections$rounds_kb$)
