insert into private.conditions (slug, condition_id, name, case_suitable, commonness, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, triage, background) values ($rounds_kb$spinal-cord-compression$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$core-spinal-cord-compression$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Spinal cord compression$rounds_kb$, true, $rounds_kb$uncommon$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$surgery$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$nervous$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$musculoskeletal$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb${"name": "Spinal cord compression", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Back pain with neurologic deficits; students can localize the lesion and build a differential of malignancy, abscess and fracture, with urgent imaging decisions.", "kind": "disease", "category": "neurologic emergency", "organ_systems": ["nervous", "musculoskeletal"], "primary_clerkship": "neurology", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "internalMedicine", "surgery"], "commonness": "uncommon", "settings": ["emergency", "inpatient"], "is_cancer": false}$rounds_kb$::jsonb, $rounds_kb$
MeSH definition (Spinal Cord Compression): Acute and chronic conditions characterized by external mechanical compression of the SPINAL CORD due to extramedullary neoplasm; EPIDURAL ABSCESS; SPINAL FRACTURES; bony deformities of the vertebral bodies; and other conditions. Clinical manifestations vary with the anatomic site of the lesion and may include localized pain, weakness, sensory loss, incontinence, and impotence.
Related conditions (candidate look-alikes): Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis, Spinal Cord Injuries, Spinal Muscular Atrophy, Syringomyelia$rounds_kb$)
